    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Zurich Zebras centers on the elite utility of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who carries the highest daily score of 82.13. His matchup against Rogers is optimized by a highly favorable park factor (+16%) and a significant stolen base opportunity stemming from a slow-delivery pitcher (+4%), playing directly into our strategic underweighting of SB scarcity. **Trea Turner** (73.89) and **Kyle Schwarber** (70.57) round out the top tier of the lineup, both benefiting from an excellent matchup against Singer; **Trea Turner**\u2019s presence at the top of the order remains a cornerstone of our daily R and SB production, while **Kyle Schwarber** continues to provide high-leverage power upside.\n\nBeyond the headliners, **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) and **Caleb Durbin** (63.65) emerge as strong starts, with **Casey Schmitt** specifically buoyed by a wind-aided environment (+5%) and a positive platoon split against Feltner. The most difficult bench decision involved weighing **Carson Benge** (56.72) against the lower-floor projections of **Lars Nootbaar** (43.93). Despite **Lars Nootbaar** having a dynamic platoon advantage, the 38% rain risk and the relative difficulty of the Henderson matchup suppressed his score, rendering him a marginal start. We are closely monitoring the weather in that stadium; should the risk increase, he will be swapped to preserve efficiency. \n\nThe remaining roster, including **Luke Raley**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Chase Meidroth**, maintains solid, if unspectacular, expected output. **Chase Meidroth** faces a tough hurdle against Sandoval (2.08 xERA), though his high-order position mitigates the risk of a total collapse in scoring efficiency. We remain cautious of the bench, where names like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** are unavailable or in the minors, confirming that our current active lineup represents the optimal path for maximizing our 5x5 categorical accumulation today.",
